<%# The Stage (docs/DESIGN.md, "The Stage"): one 16:9 frame in the middle of every screen at the table, the
    same for everyone, where the game is shown: where the party is (the map, or the dungeon's floorplan,
    with the place's picture behind them when it has one), the date and the part of the day in its corner,
    and what's being said along its bottom. Display only: nothing on it is pressed; the moves are off the
    stage. Each part is replaced live (Campaign::Broadcasts), so every screen shows the same stage; a
    battle plays on the same frame, on its own page. %>
<section class="stage stage--table" id="stage" aria-label="Stage" data-controller="stage-fit" data-stage-fit-below-value="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:caption, true) ? 48 : 0 %>">
  <div class="stage__frame">
    <%= render "campaigns/tables/scene", campaign: campaign %>
    <div class="stage__map">
      <%= render "campaigns/tables/floorplan", campaign: campaign, gm: gm %>
      <%= render "campaigns/maps/canvas", campaign: campaign, gm: gm %>
    </div>
    <%= render "campaigns/tables/dialogue_box", last_dialogue: last_dialogue, extra: "dialogue--stage" %>
  </div>
  <div class="stage__hud"><%= render "campaigns/tables/time", campaign: campaign %></div>
  <%# Under the frame, the links: the stage itself is never pressed. (Not on a stage-only screen.) %>
  <% if local_assigns.fetch(:caption, true) %>
  <p class="stage__caption hint">
    <%= link_to(gm ? "Edit the map / travel →" : "Open the map →", campaign_map_path(campaign)) %>
    <%= render "campaigns/tables/here", campaign: campaign %>
    <% if gm && campaign.map_nodes.where(visible: false).exists? %>
      <span class="gm-only-hint">Faded places are hidden: only you see them.</span>
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <% end %>
</section>
